  "result": "The `drv.motion.u_turn` concept passed the gate with `OK` on the first of 6 runs (3 witnesses, reading one atom).\n\n**Body:** the size of the car's heading change over the last `window` seconds must be at least `min_angle` and at most `max_angle`. I take the absolute value of `prim_heading_change`, because \"magnitude\" means a turn to either side counts, and both ends of the range count. The body is just this check at each moment, so it starts holding when the turn reaches the range, keeps holding while it stays there, and stops when it leaves. Nothing earlier than the window is looked at. The record left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses:** I set the window to 10 s and the range to 150°–210°. Each scenario has one car seen once a second for 30 s, and is judged from 17 s to 21 s so that no look-back window runs past the start of the trace.\n- **holds:** a three-point turn: forward left, backing, then forward left again, at 30°/s over six observations. That is 180° in total, so the result is compliant.\n- **fails:** a left turn at a junction, 90° in total, so the result is violated.\n- **blind:** the holds trace with `kin.yaw_rate` declared absent. The result is unknown, and only because of the missing yaw rate.\n\nOne thing was blocked: a shell command to list the Core directory needed approval and was denied, since the shell may only run the gate command. I read the Core files I needed (the heading-change primitive, how look-back windows are measured, and how a witness's window is judged) with the Read tool and `grep` instead.\n\n`task_result.md` with the run log and these choices is in the working directory.",
